``dxtbx.nexus.get_frame_counts``/``get_available_frame_count``: report how many leading frames of a live NXmx master are actually written to disk, resolving the DLS ``.``-self + external-link VDS layout. Detector data files are allocated at their full block extent up front, so availability is judged from the number of written per-frame chunks rather than the (static) dataset extent, under an SWMR read or once the writer has closed the file. New ``dev.dxtbx.image_availability`` CLI live-monitors this, and ``dev.dxtbx.simulate_collection`` duplicates a master's structure and fills it via SWMR to test it.
